+# Approve button: why the label disappears, and the fix
+
+## What DaisyUI does with `btn loading`
+
+In current DaisyUI (v4/v5), `loading` is **not** a `btn` modifier — it's a
+standalone spinner *component*. Its CSS looks roughly like this:
+
+```css
+.loading {
+  pointer-events: none;
+  display: inline-block;
+  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;          /* force square */
+  width: 1.5rem;               /* fixed size */
+  background-color: currentColor;
+  -webkit-mask-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,<spinner>");
+          mask-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,<spinner>");
+  -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat; mask-repeat: no-repeat;
+  -webkit-mask-position: center;  mask-position: center;
+  -webkit-mask-size: 100%;        mask-size: 100%;
+  animation: spin 2s linear infinite; /* via loading-spinner */
+}
+```
+
+The trick is `mask-image` + `background-color: currentColor`. The element is
+painted as a solid `currentColor` rectangle, and the spinner SVG mask **clips
+that paint down to the spinner silhouette**. A CSS mask applies to the whole
+element box — including its text and child nodes — so anything that isn't
+inside the spinner shape is masked away.
+
+When you put `loading` on the `<button>` **itself**:
+
+- The button's entire rendering (background + the `"Approving..."` text) is
+  clipped to the spinner glyph. The text is still in the DOM, but it's masked
+  out — invisible. That's why the label "never shows."
+- `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1` + `width: 1.5rem` fight `btn`'s own sizing, so the
+  button collapses toward a small square. That's the **layout jump**.
+- Net effect: the whole button becomes one spinner. Reads as broken. Same on
+  desktop and mobile because it's pure CSS masking, not a breakpoint issue.
+
+(Historical note: in DaisyUI v2/v3, `btn loading` *did* work as expected —
+it added a spinner via `::before` and kept the label. The teammate likely
+copied a v2/v3-era snippet into a v4/v5 codebase, where `loading` was
+redesigned into a masked component.)
+
+## The idiomatic fix
+
+Don't put `loading` on the button. Render a **separate spinner element**
+(`loading loading-spinner`) *inside* the button, next to the text. `btn` is a
+flex container with a gap, so the spinner sits inline before the label with
+correct spacing and no layout jump.
+
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isPending}>
+  {isPending && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  {isPending ? "Approving..." : "Approve"}
+</button>
+```
+
+Why this is right:
+
+- `loading loading-spinner` masks **only the `<span>`**, so the spinner is a
+  spinner and the text stays visible.
+- `loading-sm` keeps it small and inline — a spinner *next to* text, not a
+  button-sized blob.
+- The button keeps its normal `btn btn-primary` size; no collapse, no jump.
+- `disabled={isPending}` still blocks double-submits.
+- `btn`'s built-in flex gap spaces the spinner from the label automatically —
+  no manual `mr-2` needed (add `gap-2` on the button if your version doesn't
+  space it).

